## DESCRIPTION
## Taylor polynomials
## ENDDESCRIPTION

## DBsubject('Calculus - multivariable')
## DBchapter('Differentiation of multivariable functions')
## DBsection('Taylor polynomials')

################################################################

DOCUMENT();

loadMacros("PGstandard.pl", "PGchoicemacros.pl", "PGML.pl");

TEXT(beginproblem());

################################################################
#
#  Setup

$mc = new_checkbox_multiple_choice();
$mc -> qa("Which of the following are true?",
"The \( N \)th Taylor polynomial of \( f \) at \( a \) exists.",
"If \( P \) is the \( N \)th Taylor polynomial of \( f \) at \( a \) then  \( \lim_{x \to a} \dfrac{f(x) - P(x)}{||x-a||^N}=0 \).",
"If \( P \) is the 10th Taylor polynomial of \( f \) at \( a \) then \( \lim_{x \to a} \dfrac{f(x)-P(x)}{||x-a||^7} = 0 \).",
"If \( P \) is the second Taylor polynomial of \( f \) at \( a \) then \( P(a) = f(a) \), \( \nabla f(a) = \nabla P(a) \), and \( Hf(a) = HP(a) \).",
"If \( P_1 \) is the first Taylor polynomial of \( f \) at \( a \) then \( f(a) + df_a(h) = P_1(a+h) \) for all \( h \in \mathbb{R}^n \).");

$mc -> makeLast(
"The \( N \)th Taylor polynomial of \( f \) at \( a \) exists.",
"If \( P \) is the \( N \)th Taylor polynomial of \( f \) at \( a \) then  \( \lim_{x \to a} \dfrac{f(x) - P(x)}{||x-a||^N}=0 \).",
"If a polynomial \( P : \mathbb{R}^n \to \mathbb{R} \) satisfies \( \lim_{x \to a} \dfrac{f(x) - P(x)}{||x-a||^N}=0 \) then \( P \) is the \( N^\text{th} \) Taylor polynomial of \( f \) at \( a \).",
"If \( P \) is the 10th Taylor polynomial of \( f \) at \( a \) then \( \lim_{x \to a} \dfrac{f(x)-P(x)}{||x-a||^7} = 0 \).",
"If \( P \) is the second Taylor polynomial of \( f \) at \( a \) then \( P(a) = f(a) \), \( \nabla f(a) = \nabla P(a) \), and \( Hf(a) = HP(a) \).",
"If \( P_1 \) is the first Taylor polynomial of \( f \) at \( a \) then \( f(a) + df_a(h) = P_1(a+h) \) for all \( h \in \mathbb{R}^n \).");

################################################################
#
#  Text

BEGIN_PGML


Let [` f: \mathbb{R}^n \to \mathbb{R} `] be a [` C^\infty `] function. Let [` a \in \mathbb{R}^n `] and [` N \in \mathbb{N}^+ `]. [@$mc -> print_q()@]*

[@$mc -> print_a()@]*
END_PGML

################################################################
#
#  Answers

$showPartialCorrectAnswers = 0;
ANS( checkbox_cmp($mc->correct_ans()) );

ENDDOCUMENT();